Problem: For a positive integer \( n \), let \( p(n) \) denote the product of the positive integer factors of \( n \). Determine the number of factors \( n \) of 2310 for which \( p(n) \) is a perfect square.

Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.<|im_end|>
